# Architecture Rules

## Directory Boundaries
- `app/`: route segments, layouts, route handlers only.
- `src/features/*`: feature-specific UI + orchestration logic.
- `src/components/*`: shared reusable components only.
- `src/services/*`: API/data access boundaries.
- `src/lib/*`: shared pure utilities (no feature coupling).
- `src/types/*`: shared types.
- `src/config/*`: runtime/static app config.
- `src/constants/*`: constant maps and enums.

## Dependency Direction
- `app` -> `src/features` and `src/components`.
- `src/features` -> `src/components`, `src/services`, `src/lib`, `src/types`, `src/constants`.
- `src/components` must not import from `src/features`.
- `src/lib` must not import from `src/features` or `src/components`.

## Implementation Constraints
- Prefer feature colocation for business logic.
- Keep pages thin; push logic into `src/features`.
- Avoid duplicate utilities; consolidate in `src/lib`.

## Import Conventions
- Use `@/*` alias (mapped to `src/*`) for all internal imports.
- Keep relative imports local within same folder subtree.
